  "arxiv_id": "2606.30265",
  "title": "When Is a Draft Accepted? A Theory of Acceptance in Speculative Decoding",
  "summary": "Replaces classical stochastic analysis of speculative decoding with an acceptance theory for greedy decoding, relaxed acceptance, and candidate trees. It introduces a theoretical certification framework without new infrastructure, rather than a new acceleration method. It can inform implementation decisions but does not itself make a system faster; the analysis characterizes drafter-token acceptance and is evaluated on Qwen3 models.",
  "rationale": "Theory explaining existing acceptance criteria, without a new method or quantified speed gain to adopt on a small setup.",
